  "limits": [
    "Not embedded or activated in WebMux. Owner authorization, durable manifest/journal composition, caller/UI conversion and frozen-plan revalidation remain open.",
    "The explicit native conversation UUID is syntax/policy checked, not authorized by the wrapper. The manager/caller must select and verify the original conversation and immutable occupant.",
    "Recovery requires supported checked Stop of the original idle seat after provider loss, then the single-seat launch endpoint using its explicit snapshot. Whole-rig restore refuses a live sibling; the macOS account-restart observer refuses unverified process settings. Neither refusal was bypassed.",
    "Native policies are documented per-thread workspace overrides projected through the existing native account. Selected/default owner workspace configuration, named permission graphs, Linux/Windows, read-only/full-access execution and non-default tier remain unqualified here.",
    "Only the network-disabled case tests duplicate native recovery POSTs. Both positive cases test original member.add replay after recovery without another provider launch.",
    "Missing-conversation control deliberately records an unused UUID through the supported operator CLI before snapshot capture. It retains all original conversation data; it does not simulate physical deletion/corruption of native storage.",
    "No provider-loss creation/decision/recovery UI, manager-process-loss or host-reboot acceptance claim. All roadmap/review/CI/audit/release gates remain open."
  ]
